response:
In Italy the community of property ends :

* by a declaration of absence or presumed death of one spouse, by annulment, by dissolution or termination of the civil effects of the marriage, by legal separation, by judicial separation of property, by a conventional change of the property regime, or by the bankruptcy of one spouse;  

* in the case of legal separation, the community is dissolved either on the date the president of the court authorises the spouses to live separately or on the date the minutes of a consensual separation before the president are signed and approved; the order is then communicated to the civil registrar for registration;  

* for companies managed jointly by the spouses and created after the marriage, the community may be dissolved by the spouses’ agreement (observing the form of art. 162), by public deed, or by a declaration in the marriage certificate.  

All of the above are set out in the Italian Civil Code, art. 191 [S1].

